    axes: { harm: 0, pitch: 1, ornament: 1, meter: 1, density: 1, transmission: 1, improv: 1, soundTech: 0, intensity: 2, voice: 2, timbre: 1, percussion: 2, cyclicity: 1 },
    description: 'Late-1990s-and-early-2000s American heavy-rock subgenre integrating hip-hop rhythmic-vocal influence, down-tuned-seven-string-guitar metal aesthetic, and confessional-aggressive-personal-trauma lyrical content. Korn (Bakersfield, 1993-onward), Deftones, Limp Bizkit, Slipknot, and Linkin Park constitute the canonical roster. The 1998 Family Values Tour consolidated the genre\'s commercial peak.',
    exemplars: ['Korn', 'Deftones', 'Limp Bizkit', 'Slipknot', 'Linkin Park', 'System of a Down'],
