    axes: { harm: 1, pitch: 1, ornament: 1, meter: 1, density: 2, transmission: 1, improv: 1, soundTech: 0, intensity: 1, voice: 2, timbre: 1, percussion: 2, cyclicity: 1 },
    description: 'Early-1990s-and-onward American heavy-rock subgenre integrating hip-hop vocal-delivery and rhythmic-foundation with heavy-metal guitar-bass-drum aesthetic. Rage Against the Machine (Los Angeles, 1991-2000, 2007-onward) is the canonical type-specimen, with explicit revolutionary-political lyric content; the parallel Body Count (Ice-T project) and (later) the 2000s wave of Hed PE and Sevendust extended the genre.',
