    axes: { harm: 1, pitch: 1, ornament: 1, meter: 1, density: 2, transmission: 1, improv: 2, soundTech: 0, intensity: 2, voice: 2, timbre: 1, percussion: 2, cyclicity: 1 },
    description: 'Mid-1980s-and-onward American rock subgenre integrating funk slap-bass and rhythmic-syncopation with heavy-rock guitar-bass-drum aesthetic. Red Hot Chili Peppers (Los Angeles, 1983-onward) inaugurated the canonical sound; Faith No More, Primus, Mr. Bungle, and Fishbone constitute the canonical roster. Distinguished from broader rock by funk metal\'s explicit syncopated-funk-bass emphasis.',
