    description: 'Subgenre of deep-and-tech-house emerging from late 2000s through 2010s, integrating West, Central, and Southern African percussion-and-vocal influences into deep-house structural-and-tempo framework (118-126 BPM). Black Coffee (South African DJ-producer Nkosinathi Maphumulo) inaugurated the international Afro house ambassador role through his 2005-onward career; Themba, Caiiro, Da Capo, and the broader Innervisions, Get Physical, and Stay True Sounds labels anchor the canonical sound.',
    exemplars: ['Black Coffee', 'Themba', 'Caiiro', 'Da Capo', '&ME', 'Stay True Sounds'],
