    axes: { harm: 0, pitch: 1, ornament: 1, meter: 1, density: 1, transmission: 1, improv: 0, soundTech: 1, intensity: 1, voice: 2, timbre: 1, percussion: 1, cyclicity: 0 },
    description: 'Early-2010s electronic subgenre developed through online-distributed-production scene integrating chopped-and-screwed Houston hip-hop slowed-down vocal-aesthetic, dark-occult-Goth-aesthetic, and trip-hop-influenced atmospheric production. Salem (Detroit), Crystal Castles (associated), oOoOO, White Ring, and the broader Tri Angle Records and Disaro Records rosters anchor the canonical sound. Notable for its triangle, cross, and runic-Unicode visual-aesthetic.',
    exemplars: ['Salem', 'oOoOO', 'White Ring', 'Pictureplane', 'Crystal Castles (adjacent)', 'Tri Angle Records'],
    status: 'documented',
