    axes: { harm: 0, pitch: 1, ornament: 1, meter: 2, density: 2, transmission: 1, improv: 1, soundTech: 1, intensity: 2, voice: -1, timbre: 1, percussion: 2, cyclicity: 2 },
    description: 'Late-1990s and 2000s electronic subgenre characterized by extreme-fast (200-300 BPM) chopped-Amen-break-and-other-breakbeat percussion, dense-aggressive sample-collage composition, and complex polymetric rhythmic structures. Venetian Snares (Aaron Funk, Winnipeg Canada, 2000-onward) is the canonical type-specimen; Igorrr, Drumcorps, Knifehandchop, and the broader Planet Mu and Hymen Records label rosters constitute the canonical roster.',
    exemplars: ['Venetian Snares', 'Igorrr', 'Drumcorps', 'Knifehandchop', 'Bong-Ra', 'Planet Mu Records'],
    status: 'documented',
