    axes: { harm: 1, pitch: 1, ornament: 1, meter: 2, density: 2, transmission: 1, improv: 1, soundTech: 1, intensity: 1, voice: -2, timbre: 1, percussion: 2, cyclicity: 2 },
    description: 'Mid-1990s UK electronic subgenre developed by Aphex Twin (Richard D. James) and Squarepusher (Tom Jenkinson) as extreme-virtuoso drum-and-bass adjacent style with hyperactive drum-machine programming, complex polymetric rhythmic-structures, and integration with broader IDM compositional aesthetic. Aphex Twin\'s Hangable Auto Bulb (1995) and Squarepusher\'s Hard Normal Daddy (1997) constitute canonical type-specimens.',
    exemplars: ['Aphex Twin', 'Squarepusher', 'µ-Ziq', 'Luke Vibert', 'Plug (Luke Vibert)', 'Rephlex Records'],
