    description: 'Early-2010s electronic subgenre integrating Atlanta-trap production-aesthetic with EDM-festival big-room structural framework. Baauer\'s "Harlem Shake" (2012, viral 2013) inaugurated the broader commercial visibility; Diplo, RL Grime, UZ, Flosstradamus, and the broader Mad Decent label roster defined the canonical EDM-trap roster. Distinguished from Atlanta trap proper by festival trap\'s explicit instrumental-EDM-functional emphasis over rap-vocal-feature.',
    exemplars: ['Baauer', 'Diplo', 'RL Grime', 'UZ', 'Flosstradamus', 'Mad Decent Records'],
    status: 'documented',
    crossRefs: ['electronicDance.house'],
