    axes: { harm: 1, pitch: 1, ornament: 1, meter: 1, density: 2, transmission: 1, improv: 1, soundTech: 1, intensity: 0, voice: 1, timbre: 1, percussion: 2, cyclicity: 2 },
    description: 'Mid-2010s vaporwave-derived electronic subgenre integrating French house, disco, and Japanese city-pop sampling into accessible, uplifting dance-music. Saint Pepsi (later Skylar Spence), Yung Bae, Macross 82-99, and the broader Business Casual and Local Business label rosters anchor the canonical future funk aesthetic. Distinguished from broader vaporwave by future funk\'s explicit dance-functional and uplifting (vs vaporwave\'s ironic-melancholic) emotional register.',
