    axes: { harm: 2, pitch: 1, ornament: 1, meter: 1, density: 1, transmission: 1, improv: 1, soundTech: 1, intensity: 1, voice: 2, timbre: 1, percussion: 2, cyclicity: 0 },
    description: '2010s and 2020s R&B subgenre characterized by virtuoso-instrumental playing (especially electric bass), jazz-and-fusion harmonic complexity, lo-fi-and-experimental production aesthetic, and explicit Los-Angeles-Brainfeeder-scene cultural affiliation. Thundercat (Stephen Bruner, born 1984) anchored the canonical sound through Drunk (2017); Steve Lacy (The Internet), Hiatus Kaiyote (Australian, parallel scene), and the broader Brainfeeder, Stones Throw, and Anticon label rosters extended the genre.',
    exemplars: ['Thundercat', 'Steve Lacy', 'Hiatus Kaiyote', 'The Internet', 'Anderson .Paak', 'Brainfeeder Records'],
    status: 'documented',
