    description: '1990s indie rock subgenre developed in Montreal, Chicago, and Glasgow scenes characterized by extended-instrumental composition (typically 10-25 minute pieces), gradual-crescendo dynamic-architecture, classical-art-music-influenced harmonic vocabulary, and minimal-to-absent vocal-content. Godspeed You! Black Emperor (Montreal, 1994-onward) is the canonical type-specimen with F♯ A♯ ∞ (1997) and Lift Your Skinny Fists Like Antennas to Heaven (2000); Mogwai (Glasgow), Explosions in the Sky (Austin), Sigur Rós (Iceland), and Tortoise (Chicago) constitute the canonical international roster.',
