    description: 'Early-2000s indie rock subgenre revisiting late-1970s and early-1980s post-punk aesthetic (Joy Division, Wire, Gang of Four, the Fall) with explicit angular-guitar-and-driving-bass arrangement. Interpol (NYC 2002-onward), Franz Ferdinand (Glasgow), Bloc Party, the Editors, the Killers, the Strokes (parallel garage-rock-revival), and the broader 2002-2006 NME-promoted UK-American post-punk-revival wave consolidated the canonical sound.',
    exemplars: ['Interpol', 'Franz Ferdinand', 'Bloc Party', 'Editors', 'The Killers', 'The Strokes'],
