    description: '1980s and 1990s European indie subgenre developed from post-punk into more atmospheric, gothic, and synth-emphasis direction. Dead Can Dance (Australian-British 1981-onward), The Cure (transitional), Lycia, Black Tape for a Blue Girl, Diary of Dreams, and the broader Projekt Records (American) and 4AD Records (British) label rosters anchor the canonical darkwave roster.',
