    axes: { harm: -2, pitch: 0, ornament: 1, meter: -2, density: -2, transmission: -2, improv: 1, soundTech: -2, intensity: 0, voice: 2, timbre: 0, percussion: -2, cyclicity: -1 },
    description: 'The Albanian vajtim (lament) tradition continuous from medieval Albanian rural practice through 19th-20th century continuous performance; particularly preserved in Northern Albanian highland zones (Mirdita, Dukagjin, Pukë) where the gjamë (the men\'s breast-beating funeral-mourning) and the women\'s vajtim are structurally distinct practices, and in Albanian-language Kosovo and Southern-Italian Arbëresh diaspora communities. Defined by free-meter melismatic Albanian-vocal phrasing, Albanian-Balkan modal vocabulary with Eastern-modal inflection, sob-glottalization vocal technique, Albanian-language text register, women\'s-voice primary tradition for the vajtim (men\'s gjamë is a separate gendered practice featuring ritualized breast-beating and rhythmic crying). Distinguished from Greek moirológi by Albanian linguistic register and from Sardinian atítidu by Balkan-not-Mediterranean modal-vocabulary lineage.',
    exemplars: ['Northern-Albanian Mirdita vajtim (field-recordings)', 'Marie Logoreci — folk-revival vajtim recordings', 'Albanian-Kosovar vajtim tradition (1990s-2000s ethnographic documentation)', 'Arbëresh-Italian vajtim (Southern-Italian Albanian-language diaspora)', 'Eli Fara — modern Albanian lament-adjacent vocal recordings'],
