    description: 'The French-language children\'s play-song and counting-out-rhyme (comptine) tradition continuous from medieval-and-early-modern French folk-play-song origins through 19th-century French-Republic school-curriculum codification into modern continuous French-and-French-Canadian-and-Francophone-African childhood-practice. Defined by narrow-range melodic vocabulary, characteristic French-language text register with the syllabic-stress pattern of French (final-syllable stress) shaping musical-phrase delivery, action-coordination structure for circle-game and finger-game and counting-out applications, characteristic French-folk-modal pentatonic-leaning vocabulary, durable oral transmission. The canonical French nursery-rhyme corpus includes Frère Jacques (Brother John), Sur le pont d\'Avignon (On the Avignon Bridge), Au clair de la lune (By the Light of the Moon), Alouette (Lark, with French-Canadian skinning-the-lark text-tradition).',
