    description: 'The Sami yoik (joik) tradition continuous from premodern Sami reindeer-herding-and-hunting-and-fishing practice across the Sápmi-region of northern Norway, Sweden, Finland, and Russia through colonial-era Christianization-suppression (the Sami yoik was actively suppressed by Lutheran-Norwegian-and-Swedish missionary-and-state-policy from 17th-19th centuries with documented yoiking-prohibition laws) continuous through 20th-century revival. The yoik is the canonical Sami-vocal-genre integrating animal-tracking (the yoiker performs a yoik OF the animal — not ABOUT it — that captures the essence of the reindeer, bear, wolf, or other game-animal), person-naming, and place-naming functions. Defined by unaccompanied solo-vocal recitative arrangement, Sami-language text register, narrow-range pentatonic-leaning melodic vocabulary, characteristic free-meter recitative-style.',
    exemplars: ['Mari Boine — canonical modern Sami yoik-vocalist', 'Wimme Saari — Finnish-Sami canonical yoik', 'Nils-Aslak Valkeapää — canonical Sami yoik-poet', 'Inga Juuso — canonical traditional Sami-Norwegian yoik', 'Modern Sami yoik-revival continuous-living tradition'],
