    description: 'The Sardinian boci de tela ("weaving songs") and broader Sardinian women\'s-domestic-textile-labor song tradition continuous from medieval-Sardinian-rural domestic-textile labor practice through 19th-20th century continuous performance into modern Sardinian-folk-revival; the Sardinian weaving-song integrates the back-strap-loom-and-vertical-loom textile-labor (Sardinian-traditional carpets and tapestries are documented as among the most-elaborate Mediterranean-textile traditions) with extensive narrative-and-improvised-song. The Sardinian women\'s domestic-textile-song tradition is distinct from the Sardinian a tenore men\'s-polyphony tradition but shares the broader Sardinian-traditional vocal-aesthetic and modal-vocabulary. Defined by unaccompanied women\'s-solo-or-small-group vocal arrangement, Sardinian-language text register, Mediterranean-polyphonic-modal vocabulary, characteristic narrow-range narrative-style.',
